From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client: bare_app save slots and on-screen keyboard

The console has no keyboard, so typing a save's name was the hard part
of saving. When bare_app runs the client (see 0001):

- the autosave after each turn is one file, Saves/Autosave, replaced
  every turn and listed first; VCMI's dated autosave folders are not made;
- the save screen lists ten slots (Saves/Slot01..Slot10), empty ones too,
  instead of the name field; an empty slot shows the game being saved,
  a full one asks before it is overwritten, and the "saved" message
  names the slot instead of the file;
- the load screen shows the autosave and the slots first, by their
  names ("Autosave", "Slot 3"), then any other saves;
- a text input that the player clicks (a town's name, a search box,
  numbers) opens an on-screen keyboard over the other half of the
  screen: digits, Russian (when the game is in Russian) and Latin
  letters, capitals, space. The stick's cursor or the D-pad picks a key
  and A presses it; B is "done", Select cancels, X erases. As on mobile,
  an input that gets focus by itself does not open it.

Also fixed on the way, for everybody: a text input with its own
confirmation (a town's name) could not be clicked again once a window
had been over it, since its deactivation dropped its clicks for good.

Upstream: not applicable (SDK-specific)
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
